{"ts":"2026-04-26T02:38:00.790Z","stream":"stdout","chunk":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_6kb4yk9ovh6l_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→# Labebe AI Design Studio — Boss Demo Pack\\n     2→**Lane:** Claude Code (Paperclip `claude_local` runtime — local CLI/client, not hosted)\\n     3→**Model from run evidence:** `MiniMax-M2.7` (`provider: anthropic`)\\n     4→**Artifact path:** `outputs/claude_code_demo.md`\\n     5→**Evidence base:** Local files only — no internet sources, no fabricated metrics\\n     6→\\n     7→---\\n     8→\\n     9→## Executive Demo Narrative\\n    10→\\n    11→**What this demo proves:** Paperclip is the local control plane for Labebe AI Design Studio — not a magic AI box, but an orchestration and governance layer that organizes agents, assigns issues, executes heartbeats, captures evidence, and gates risky claims behind human review.\\n    12→\\n    13→The demo is intentionally scoped to a **deterministic process adapter** running on loopback. This is a flight simulator, not full AI reasoning. The value is in the control plane: auditable issue-to-artifact chains, skill registries, MCP tool policies, and evidence ledgers that a boss can trust without needing to verify every AI output.\\n    14→\\n    15→> *\\\"Today you will not see AI autonomously inventing and launching a toy product. You will see Paperclip run an AI team: organized, gated, evidenced, and stoppable.\\\"*\\n    16→\\n    17→**Runtime truth:** The Claude Code lane runs through Paperclip's `claude_local` adapter on this machine's local CLI/client. The model evidence from the prior run confirms: `MiniMax-M2.7` (provider: `anthropic`). This is **not** an official Anthropic-hosted model — it is the local runtime as configured on this machine. The Kimi lane runs the same Paperclip control plane with the `kimi_cli` adapter. The duel compares output quality, not brand prestige.\\n    18→\\n    19→---\\n    20→\\n    21→## What The Boss Should See In 90 Seconds\\n    22→\\n    23→### 0:00–0:20 — The Setup\\n    24→Show the Paperclip company dashboard at `http://127.0.0.1:3100`.\\n    25→- Company: **Labebe AI Design Studio**\\n    26→- 9 agents, all `process` adapter (deterministic, loopback)\\n    27→- 10 issues (LAB-0 through LAB-9) covering product concept pipeline\\n    28→- Skills: governance, product workflow, demo operator\\n    29→\\n    30→**Boss takeaway:** A real AI team control console, not a chatbot.\\n    31→\\n    32→### 0:20–0:40 — Live Smoke Run\\n    33→Trigger `LAB-SMOKE-001` (\\\"CASE 1 - Data Truth Guard end-to-end smoke\\\") on the Data Truth Guard agent.\\n    34→Watch the issue move: `todo → in_progress → done`.\\n    35→\\n    36→Show in real time:\\n    37→1. `paperclipCheckoutIssue` — agent claims the issue\\n    38→2. Artifact written to `outputs/case-LAB-SMOKE-001-data-truth-guard.md`\\n    39→3. `paperclipAddComment` — comment written to the issue\\n    40→4. `paperclipUpdateIssue` — status set to `done`\\n    41→\\n    42→**Boss takeaway:** Every action is issue-bound, agent-assigned, and evidenced.\\n    43→\\n    44→### 0:40–1:00 — Where The AI Cannot Go\\n    45→Show the blocked issue `LAB-7` (DFM / Safety / Cost Preflight) and the `FORBIDDEN_CLAIMS.md` list.\\n    46→- No agent can claim real customer demand, verified safety certification, or production launch date without human sign-off.\\n    47→- MCP tool policy shows: no `create agent`, no `update adapter`, no `delete company`, no `update secret`.\\n    48→\\n    49→**Boss takeaway:** Paperclip has gates, not just automation.\\n    50→\\n    51→### 1:00–1:30 — The Product Concept Pipeline\\n    52→Walk the issue tree:\\n    53→- `LAB-1` Data Truth Foundation → `LAB-2` Product Opportunity Radar → `LAB-3` VOC to Product Concept → `LAB-6` Design Director Review → `LAB-7` DFM/Safety blocked gate → `LAB-8` Asset Matrix draft\\n    54→\\n    55→Show that each stage has an owner agent, a review gate, and an artifact.\\n    56→\\n    57→**Boss takeaway:** Paperclip can orchestrate a full product concept workflow — from voice-of-customer to design review to safety preflight.\\n    58→\\n    59→---\\n    60→\\n    61→## Control Plane Architecture\\n    62→\\n    63→### Paperclip as Governance Layer\\n    64→\\n    65→```\\n    66→┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n    67→│  Paperclip Control Plane  (http://127.0.0.1:3100)  │\\n    68→│                                                     │\\n    69→│  Company: Labebe AI Design Studio                  │\\n    70→│  Company ID: 1cb6d439-2bdf-4f63-ad9a-b5326d5546df │\\n    71→│  Deployment: local_trusted / private / loopback      │\\n    72→└──────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘\\n    73→                   │\\n    74→     ┌─────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┐\\n    75→     │             │                                 │\\n    76→  ┌──▼──┐    ┌────▼────┐    ┌─────────────────┐   │\\n    77→  │Issue │    │ Skills  │    │  MCP Tool Policy │   │\\n    78→  │Tree  │    │Registry │    │  allow/deny list │   │\\n    79→  │LAB-0 │    │3 skills │    │  read-only except│   │\\n    80→     │    │    │attached│    │  LAB-SMOKE-001   │   │\\n    81→  ┌──▼────▼┐  └─────────┘    └─────────────────┘   │\\n    82→  │Agents  │                                            │\\n    83→  │ 9 ×   │                                            │\\n    84→  │process│                                            │\\n    85→  │adapter│                                            │\\n    86→  └────────┘                                            │\\n    87→```\\n    88→\\n    89→### Runtime Alias Separation\\n    90→\\n    91→| Lane | Runtime | Adapter | Model (from run evidence) | Evidence |\\n    92→|------|---------|---------|--------------------------|---------|\\n    93→| Claude Code | `claude_local` | Paperclip claude_local | `MiniMax-M2.7` (provider: `anthropic`) | `evidence/claude_run.json` |\\n    94→| Kimi | `kimi_cli` | Paperclip kimi_cli adapter | `kimi-for-coding` (self-reported via `kimi_run.json`; provider: `Moonshot AI` per Kimi artifact) | `evidence/kimi_run.json`, `outputs/kimi_demo.md` |\\n    95→\\n    96→Both lanes share the same company, same issue tree, same skill registry, same MCP policy. The runtime alias ensures lane isolation — one lane's agent config cannot affect the other's. The model name and provider are captured from actual run evidence, not assumptions.\\n    97→\\n    98→### Issue/Agent/Heartbeat/Artifact Flow\\n    99→\\n   100→```\\n   101→Issue assigned\\n   102→    │\\n   103→    ▼\\n   104→Agent heartbeat fires\\n   105→    │  (PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID injected by Paperclip)\\n   106→    ▼\\n   107→process adapter reads workspace docs\\n   108→    │\\n   109→    ▼\\n   110→Artifact written to outputs/\\n   111→    │\\n   112→    ├── Paperclip comment ← paperclipAddComment (status: Demo heartbeat completed.)\\n   113→    └── Issue status update ← paperclipUpdateIssue (target: LAB-SMOKE-001 only)\\n   114→```\\n   115→\\n   116→MCP mutations are gated by `PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID` and limited to `LAB-SMOKE-001`.\\n   117→\\n   118→### Paperclip Env Injection Contract\\n   119→\\n   120→For the process adapter to reach Paperclip, these env vars are injected at runtime by Paperclip (not stored in the portable packet):\\n   121→\\n   122→| Variable | Purpose | Stored in packet? |\\n   123→|----------|---------|------------------|\\n   124→| `PAPERCLIP_API_URL` | Loopback Paperclip API | Template only — no raw key |\\n   125→| `PAPERCLIP_API_KEY` | Local agent key | Never — lives outside packet |\\n   126→| `PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID` | Company ID | Yes (name only, not secret) |\\n   127→| `PAPERCLIP_AGENT_ID` | Agent ID for this run | Injected at runtime |\\n   128→| `PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID` | Run traceability | Injected at runtime for mutations |\\n   129→| `LABEBE_TARGET_ISSUE_IDENTIFIER` | Smoke target | Yes (value: `LAB-SMOKE-001`) |\\n   130→\\n   131→**Fact:** Raw API keys are never in the portable packet or evidence export. Evidence files use `PAPERCLIP_API_KEY` placeholder.\\n   132→\\n   133→---\\n   134→\\n   135→## Same-Goal Generation Plan\\n   136→\\n   137→Both Claude Code and Kimi lanes produce an identical-schema artifact from the same evidence base. This is a **controlled comparison**, not a race.\\n   138→\\n   139→### Shared Constraints\\n   140→- Evidence base: local files only (no internet)\\n   141→- Output schema: 12-section boss demo pack\\n   142→- Scoring rubric: `rubric_100.yaml` (100-point)\\n   143→- Target score: 95+\\n   144→\\n   145→### What Each Lane Owns\\n   146→| Concern | Claude Code | Kimi |\\n   147→|---------|-------------|------|\\n   148→| Artifact generation | `claude_code_demo.md` | `kimi_demo.md` |\\n   149→| Demo narrative script | 90-second boss walkthrough | Same |\\n   150→| Architecture accuracy | Control plane framing | Same |\\n   151→| Wow factor | Premium Labebe concept | Same |\\n   152→| Governance labels | Fact/Inference/Hypothesis | Same |\\n   153→| Model truth | `MiniMax-M2.7` from run evidence (`claude_run.json`) | `kimi-for-coding` (Kimi artifact self-report; `kimi_run.json` confirms `kimi_cli` lane) |\\n   154→\\n   155→### Verification\\n   156→The rubric has a **fail condition** on missing evidence ledger and missing self-score. Both lanes must include a completed `## Evidence Ledger` and `## Final Self-Score` section.\\n   157→\\n   158→---\\n   159→\\n   160→## The Premium Labebe Demo Concept\\n   161→\\n   162→### Elevator Pitch\\n   163→Labebe AI Design Studio is a **red-team-gated AI product design team** that turns voice-of-customer (VOC) signals, competitor data, and design briefs into concept assets — but never ships a claim, a cost figure, or a safety certification without a human gate.\\n   164→\\n   165→The product concept is a **toy/home lifestyle brand** — premium materials, modular design, parent-child interaction focus. The AI team's job is to surface opportunity and generate concepts; a human boss owns the go/no-go.\\n   166→\\n   167→### Stage Moments\\n   168→\\n   169→**Moment 1 — The Dashboard (wow):** A single Paperclip company view shows 9 agent cards, a 10-issue pipeline board, and a live heartbeat ticker. Each agent has a role, a skill set, and a current assignment. The word \\\"team\\\" is literal, not metaphorical.\\n   170→\\n   171→**Moment 2 — The Smoke Run (credibility):** A deterministic agent writes a structured artifact, posts it to Paperclip, and closes its issue — all within 30 seconds. The boss sees a complete audit trail: issue → agent → artifact → comment → status. No hand-waving.\\n   172→\\n   173→**Moment 3 — The Blocked Gate (trust):** LAB-7 is intentionally `blocked`. The DFM/Safety/Cost preflight agent cannot proceed because human review is required for safety-adjacent claims. The agent does not skip the gate; it stops and flags. This is the anti-hallucination control.\\n   174→\\n   175→**Moment 4 — The Concept Preview (aspiration):** LAB-3 through LAB-8 represent a real concept development arc — from VOC signals to product concept brief to design director review to DFM preflight to asset matrix. Pre-generated artifacts show what the pipeline *would* produce under human approval. No artifact is presented as shipped or validated.\\n   176→\\n   177→### Demo Sample Policy\\n   178→All outputs from this demo are labeled:\\n   179→- `demo_sample` — illustrative content, not production\\n   180→- `demo_policy` — governed by the demo's human-review requirements\\n   181→- `source_label: review_signal` — signals come from internal research, not live user data\\n   182→\\n   183→---\\n   184→\\n   185→## Visual And Interaction Direction\\n   186→\\n   187→### Primary Visual\\n   188→Paperclip company dashboard — board view showing issue pipeline from `LAB-0` (CEO Strategy Approval) to `LAB-9` (Boss Demo Production). Color-coded by status: `todo` (gray), `in_progress` (blue), `in_review` (yellow), `blocked` (red), `done` (green).\\n   189→\\n   190→### Interaction Sequence\\n   191→1. **Start:** Show company health endpoint → `status: ok`\\n   192→2. **Agent view:** Click Data Truth Guard → see desiredSkills, assigned issues, last heartbeat timestamp\\n   193→3. **Smoke trigger:** Click `LAB-SMOKE-001` → trigger heartbeat → watch status change\\n   194→4. **Artifact reveal:** Open `case-LAB-SMOKE-001-data-truth-guard.md` in split view alongside Paperclip issue\\n   195→5. **Blocked gate:** Show `LAB-7` in red with `blocked` status → open `FORBIDDEN_CLAIMS.md`\\n   196→6. **Concept preview:** Navigate `LAB-3` → `LAB-6` → `LAB-8` showing artifact chain\\n   197→\\n   198→### Premium Touches\\n   199→- The demo uses `labebe-ai-design-studio/workspace/outputs/` for all artifacts — not scattered temp files\\n   200→- Each artifact header contains: Paperclip issue ID, owner agent, source labels, human review required flag, output status\\n   201→- The MCP tool policy is shown as a JSON/YAML table so non-technical stakeholders can read the allow/deny\\n   202→\\n   203→---\\n   204→\\n   205→## Agent Organization And Workflow\\n   206→\\n   207→### Org Chart\\n   208→\\n   209→```\\n   210→Product Innovation Director\\n   211→├── Data Truth Guard          (LAB-1, LAB-SMOKE-001)\\n   212→├── VOC Intelligence Analyst  (LAB-3)\\n   213→├── Competitive Radar Analyst  (LAB-2)\\n   214→├── Design Strategy Agent     (LAB-4)\\n   215→├── Design Director Agent     (LAB-6)\\n   216→├── DFM & Safety Preflight    (LAB-7)  ← BLOCKED\\n   217→├── Concept-to-Market Agent   (LAB-8)\\n   218→└── Demo Producer Agent        (LAB-9)\\n   219→```\\n   220→\\n   221→### Skill Registry (3 skills, all agents attached)\\n   222→\\n   223→| Skill | Scope | Attached To |\\n   224→|-------|-------|-------------|\\n   225→| `labebe-demo-governance` | Data truth, forbidden claims, human review gates, source labels | All 9 agents |\\n   226→| `labebe-product-concept-workflow` | VOC → competitor → opportunity → concept → design review → DFM → asset matrix | 7 product/design/market agents |\\n   227→| `paperclip-demo-operator` | Heartbeat, issue selection, artifact path, demo replay | All 9 agents |\\n   228→\\n   229→**Inference:** `paperclip-create-agent` and `paperclip-create-plugin` are setup-level skills attached by Paperclip's built-in skill system. They are **not Labebe demo skills** and should not appear in demo-facing documentation as desired skills.\\n   230→\\n   231→### Collaboration Workflow\\n   232→\\n   233→```\\n   234→Product Innovation Director\\n   235→  │  assigns LAB-3 to VOC Analyst\\n   236→  ▼\\n   237→VOC Intelligence Analyst\\n   238→  │  produces voc-requirement-map\\n   239→  │  → in_review status\\n   240→  ▼\\n   241→Data Truth Guard (review gate)\\n   242→  │  checks for forbidden claims\\n   243→  │  → approves or blocks\\n   244→  ▼\\n   245→Design Strategy Agent\\n   246→  │  produces sketch-to-concept brief\\n   247→  ▼\\n   248→Design Director Agent\\n   249→  │  design review, DFM flag\\n   250→  ▼\\n   251→DFM & Safety Preflight [BLOCKED]\\n   252→  │  requires human review for safety-adjacent\\n   253→  ▼\\n   254→Demo Producer Agent\\n   255→  │  packages concept assets\\n   256→  ▼\\n   257→Boss Demo Production (LAB-9)\\n   258→  └── human approval required\\n   259→```\\n   260→\\n   261→### Handoff And Review Standards\\n   262→- **Issue assignment:** Only Product Innovation Director assigns issues; agents self-select from `todo` pool via heartbeat\\n   263→- **Artifact quality:** Each artifact must carry header: issue ID, agent, source labels, human review flag\\n   264→- **Review gates:** `LAB-1` (Data Truth) and `LAB-7` (DFM/Safety) are explicit review gates — no agent can bypass them\\n   265→- **Forbidden claims:** Agents must not output production-ready safety certifications, verified demand figures, or launch dates without explicit human sign-off\\n   266→\\n   267→---\\n   268→\\n   269→## Governance, MCP, Skills, And Secrets Policy\\n   270→\\n   271→### Governance Facts\\n   272→\\n   273→**Fact:** Paperclip version is `0.3.1 / local_trusted / private` — confirmed from local context.\\n   274→\\n   275→**Fact:** All 9 agents use `process` adapter — no paid model runtime, no external account calls.\\n   276→\\n   277→**Fact:** External accounts are **disabled** for the entire demo.\\n   278→\\n   279→**Fact:** Real customer data is **disabled** for the entire demo.\\n   280→\\n   281→**Fact:** Demo samples are allowed with explicit `demo_sample` / `demo_policy` labels.\\n   282→\\n   283→**Fact:** Human review is **required** for: strategy, opportunity, safety, cost, compliance-adjacent language, external publication.\\n   284→\\n   285→### MCP Tool Policy\\n   286→\\n   287→The MCP tool policy (`configs/mcp-tool-policy.yaml`) is an audit contract. It does not alter Paperclip server code.\\n   288→\\n   289→**Default:** `deny`\\n   290→\\n   291→**Allowed read-only** (no run ID required):\\n   292→- `paperclipMe`, `paperclipInboxLite`\\n   293→- `paperclipListAgents`, `paperclipGetAgent`\\n   294→- `paperclipListIssues`, `paperclipGetIssue`\\n   295→- `paperclipGetHeartbeatContext`\\n   296→- `paperclipListComments`, `paperclipGetComment`\\n   297→- `paperclipListIssueApprovals`\\n   298→- `paperclipListDocuments`, `paperclipGetDocument`\\n   299→- `paperclipListProjects`, `paperclipGetProject`\\n   300→- `paperclipListGoals`, `paperclipGetGoal`\\n   301→- `paperclipListApprovals`, `paperclipGetApproval`\\n   302→- `paperclipGetApprovalIssues`, `paperclipListApprovalComments`\\n   303→\\n   304→**Allowed mutation** (run ID required, `LAB-SMOKE-001` only):\\n   305→- `paperclipCheckoutIssue`\\n   306→- `paperclipAddComment` (marker: `Demo heartbeat completed.`)\\n   307→- `paperclipUpdateIssue` (status: `in_progress` or `done` only)\\n   308→\\n   309→**Always denied:**\\n   310→- `paperclipCreateIssue`, `paperclipReleaseIssue